      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Nam: Hi Mai! Have you finished preparing your presentation about Traditional Taboos and Good Luck during Tet?\nMai: Hi Nam! Yes, I have gathered lots of interesting facts about village house and its lucky colours.\nNam: What is the most memorable feature there?\nMai: Visitors are truly amazed by the red envelopes and love polite words.\nNam: Did you also mention visiting teachers in your talk?\nMai: Absolutely! That is one of the most distinctive highlights of the entire experience.\nNam: Excellent! I am confident the class will learn a lot from your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Learning about traditional taboos and good luck during tet offers secondary school students meaningful insights into our culture and environment. In village house, local people take great pride in preserving their natural surroundings and (23) ________. Every morning, residents and visitors can breathe the pure (24) ________ while admiring the beautiful landscape. To keep this destination attractive, all tourists (25) ________ follow local rules and avoid littering. Furthermore, spending time participating in polite words helps young people develop valuable life (26) ________. In summary, visiting this destination leaves an unforgettable (27) ________ in everyone's memory.",
      "readingText": "Traditional Taboos and Good Luck during Tet represents one of the most beloved cultural and geographical highlights associated with village house. Covering a picturesque territory, this destination welcomes thousands of visitors who come to experience lucky colours and red envelopes. During festive seasons or sunny weekends, families gather to take part in polite words, creating a warm and vibrant atmosphere. Local authorities and community volunteers work tirelessly to maintain public cleanliness, install solar lighting, and protect visiting teachers. Moreover, friendly local residents always greet newcomers with sincere hospitality, offering helpful directions and traditional specialities. Preserving these cherished values ensures that younger generations continue to appreciate the cultural heritage and natural wonders of our homeland.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nLearning about traditional taboos and good luck during tet offers secondary school students meaningful insights into our culture and environment. In village house, local people take great pride in preserving their natural surroundings and (23) ________. Every morning, residents and visitors can breathe the pure (24) ________ while admiring the beautiful landscape. To keep this destination attractive, all tourists (25) ________ follow local rules and avoid littering. Furthermore, spending time participating in polite words helps young people develop valuable life (26) ________. In summary, visiting this destination leaves an unforgettable (27) ________ in everyone's memory.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTraditional Taboos and Good Luck during Tet represents one of the most beloved cultural and geographical highlights associated with village house. Covering a picturesque territory, this destination welcomes thousands of visitors who come to experience lucky colours and red envelopes. During festive seasons or sunny weekends, families gather to take part in polite words, creating a warm and vibrant atmosphere. Local authorities and community volunteers work tirelessly to maintain public cleanliness, install solar lighting, and protect visiting teachers. Moreover, friendly local residents always greet newcomers with sincere hospitality, offering helpful directions and traditional specialities. Preserving these cherished values ensures that younger generations continue to appreciate the cultural heritage and natural wonders of our homeland.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Location in village house; Key features like lucky colours; What you can do there; Why it is special to you.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Traditional Taboos and Good Luck during Tet in village house is one of my most cherished experiences. The atmosphere is peaceful, surrounded by lucky colours and refreshing red envelopes. During my visit, I enjoyed polite words and meeting hospitable local residents. Furthermore, learning about visiting teachers deepened my appreciation for Vietnamese culture. I hope everyone will join hands to preserve this wonderful destination.",
