      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Nam: Hi Mai! What cultural heritage or culinary topic are you reviewing for English class?\nMai: Hi Nam! I am presenting about Quang Nam Noodles (Mi Quang) and Regional Flavours at Da Nang street food.\nNam: What is the most remarkable aspect of this tradition?\nMai: Everyone appreciates flat turmeric noodles and enjoys garnishing herbs.\nNam: How does it reflect the cultural identity of our people?\nMai: It highlights roasted peanuts and shrimp and showcases the authentic value of toasted sesame crackers.\nNam: That is wonderful! You will definitely achieve a high grade for your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Vietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying quang nam noodles (mi quang) and regional flavours, students discover how Da Nang street food preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering garnishing herbs requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire flat turmeric noodles, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Quang Nam Noodles (Mi Quang) and Regional Flavours represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Da Nang street food. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined flat turmeric noodles and roasted peanuts and shrimp, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in garnishing herbs, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard toasted sesame crackers to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying quang nam noodles (mi quang) and regional flavours, students discover how Da Nang street food preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering garnishing herbs requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire flat turmeric noodles, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nQuang Nam Noodles (Mi Quang) and Regional Flavours represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Da Nang street food. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined flat turmeric noodles and roasted peanuts and shrimp, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in garnishing herbs, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard toasted sesame crackers to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Location in Da Nang street food; Key ingredients or artistic features; How it is practiced; Why it is meaningful.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Quang Nam Noodles (Mi Quang) and Regional Flavours at Da Nang street food is one of my favourite cultural experiences. It showcases flat turmeric noodles and reflects the profound wisdom of our ancestors. When engaging in garnishing herbs, visitors discover how roasted peanuts and shrimp has been preserved across generations. Furthermore, safeguarding toasted sesame crackers helps younger people maintain a strong cultural identity. I am very proud of this Vietnamese heritage.",
