      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Phong: Hi Lan! What cultural heritage or culinary topic are you reviewing for English class?\nLan: Hi Phong! I am presenting about The Secrets of Making Nam Dan Soy Sauce (Tuong) at Nghe An countryside.\nPhong: What is the most remarkable aspect of this tradition?\nLan: Everyone appreciates fermented roasted soybeans and enjoys stirring golden sauce.\nPhong: How does it reflect the cultural identity of our people?\nLan: It highlights ceramic earthen jars and showcases the authentic value of traditional recipe.\nPhong: That is wonderful! You will definitely achieve a high grade for your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Vietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying the secrets of making nam dan soy sauce (tuong), students discover how Nghe An countryside preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering stirring golden sauce requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire fermented roasted soybeans, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The Secrets of Making Nam Dan Soy Sauce (Tuong) represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Nghe An countryside. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined fermented roasted soybeans and ceramic earthen jars, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in stirring golden sauce, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard traditional recipe to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying the secrets of making nam dan soy sauce (tuong), students discover how Nghe An countryside preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering stirring golden sauce requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire fermented roasted soybeans, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Secrets of Making Nam Dan Soy Sauce (Tuong) represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Nghe An countryside. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined fermented roasted soybeans and ceramic earthen jars, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in stirring golden sauce, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard traditional recipe to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Location in Nghe An countryside; Key ingredients or artistic features; How it is practiced; Why it is meaningful.",
      "sampleWritingText": "The Secrets of Making Nam Dan Soy Sauce (Tuong) at Nghe An countryside is one of my favourite cultural experiences. It showcases fermented roasted soybeans and reflects the profound wisdom of our ancestors. When engaging in stirring golden sauce, visitors discover how ceramic earthen jars has been preserved across generations. Furthermore, safeguarding traditional recipe helps younger people maintain a strong cultural identity. I am very proud of this Vietnamese heritage.",
