      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Nam: Hi Mai! What cultural heritage or culinary topic are you reviewing for English class?\nMai: Hi Nam! I am presenting about Ethnic Bamboo Instruments and Dan T'rung Melodies at Central Highlands.\nNam: What is the most remarkable aspect of this tradition?\nMai: Everyone appreciates hollow bamboo tubes and enjoys playing tribal tunes.\nNam: How does it reflect the cultural identity of our people?\nMai: It highlights resonant mountain echoes and showcases the authentic value of wooden mallets.\nNam: That is wonderful! You will definitely achieve a high grade for your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Vietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying ethnic bamboo instruments and dan t'rung melodies, students discover how Central Highlands preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering playing tribal tunes requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire hollow bamboo tubes, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Ethnic Bamboo Instruments and Dan T'rung Melodies represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Central Highlands. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined hollow bamboo tubes and resonant mountain echoes, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in playing tribal tunes, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard wooden mallets to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying ethnic bamboo instruments and dan t'rung melodies, students discover how Central Highlands preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering playing tribal tunes requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire hollow bamboo tubes, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nEthnic Bamboo Instruments and Dan T'rung Melodies represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Central Highlands. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined hollow bamboo tubes and resonant mountain echoes, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in playing tribal tunes, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard wooden mallets to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Location in Central Highlands; Key ingredients or artistic features; How it is practiced; Why it is meaningful.",
      "sampleWritingText": "Ethnic Bamboo Instruments and Dan T'rung Melodies at Central Highlands is one of my favourite cultural experiences. It showcases hollow bamboo tubes and reflects the profound wisdom of our ancestors. When engaging in playing tribal tunes, visitors discover how resonant mountain echoes has been preserved across generations. Furthermore, safeguarding wooden mallets helps younger people maintain a strong cultural identity. I am very proud of this Vietnamese heritage.",
