      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Nam: Hi Mai! What cultural tradition or lifestyle are you discussing in English class?\nMai: Hi Nam! I am presenting about Nomadic Pastoral Lifestyles on the Mongolian Steppes at Mongolian grassland.\nNam: What is the most fascinating aspect of this custom?\nMai: Anthropologists and participants are intrigued by circular felt yurt tents and enjoy riding horses across plains.\nNam: How does it preserve cultural heritage or improve well-being?\nMai: It reinforces free-roaming horse herds and honors the spiritual value of milking mare cattle.\nNam: Wonderful! That provides an insightful perspective on cultural diversity.",
      "clozeText": "Understanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Mongolian grassland, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving circular felt yurt tents and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in riding horses across plains, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating free-roaming horse herds helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing milking mare cattle strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Nomadic Pastoral Lifestyles on the Mongolian Steppes exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Mongolian grassland. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies circular felt yurt tents and reflects free-roaming horse herds, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in riding horses across plains maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize milking mare cattle as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nUnderstanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Mongolian grassland, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving circular felt yurt tents and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in riding horses across plains, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating free-roaming horse herds helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing milking mare cattle strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nNomadic Pastoral Lifestyles on the Mongolian Steppes exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Mongolian grassland. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies circular felt yurt tents and reflects free-roaming horse herds, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in riding horses across plains maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize milking mare cattle as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Features of Mongolian grassland; Key customs like circular felt yurt tents; Why milking mare cattle is respected; Your reflection on preserving heritage.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Nomadic Pastoral Lifestyles on the Mongolian Steppes is an extraordinary cultural treasure. Located in Mongolian grassland, it embodies circular felt yurt tents and illustrates how communities harmoniously interact with their environment. Practicing riding horses across plains instills profound moral values and preserves free-roaming horse herds. Moreover, honoring milking mare cattle reinforces our ancestral roots. I believe youth should actively champion the preservation of this cherished heritage.",
