      "audioScript": "Phong: Hi Lan! What cultural tradition or lifestyle are you discussing in English class?\nLan: Hi Phong! I am presenting about Minimalist Living: Simplifying Modern Teenage Possessions at tidy student bedroom.\nPhong: What is the most fascinating aspect of this custom?\nLan: Anthropologists and participants are intrigued by clutter-free study desks and enjoy donating redundant clothes.\nPhong: How does it preserve cultural heritage or improve well-being?\nLan: It reinforces mindful secondhand shopping and honors the spiritual value of wooden bookshelf.\nPhong: Wonderful! That provides an insightful perspective on cultural diversity.",
      "clozeText": "Understanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In tidy student bedroom, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving clutter-free study desks and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in donating redundant clothes, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating mindful secondhand shopping helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing wooden bookshelf strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Minimalist Living: Simplifying Modern Teenage Possessions exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in tidy student bedroom. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies clutter-free study desks and reflects mindful secondhand shopping, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in donating redundant clothes maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize wooden bookshelf as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nUnderstanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In tidy student bedroom, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving clutter-free study desks and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in donating redundant clothes, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating mindful secondhand shopping helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing wooden bookshelf strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nMinimalist Living: Simplifying Modern Teenage Possessions exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in tidy student bedroom. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies clutter-free study desks and reflects mindful secondhand shopping, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in donating redundant clothes maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize wooden bookshelf as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Features of tidy student bedroom; Key customs like clutter-free study desks; Why wooden bookshelf is respected; Your reflection on preserving heritage.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Minimalist Living: Simplifying Modern Teenage Possessions is an extraordinary cultural treasure. Located in tidy student bedroom, it embodies clutter-free study desks and illustrates how communities harmoniously interact with their environment. Practicing donating redundant clothes instills profound moral values and preserves mindful secondhand shopping. Moreover, honoring wooden bookshelf reinforces our ancestral roots. I believe youth should actively champion the preservation of this cherished heritage.",
