      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Nam: Hi Mai! What cultural tradition or lifestyle are you discussing in English class?\nMai: Hi Nam! I am presenting about The Ede Matriarchal Heritage and Communal Longhouses at Dak Lak plateau.\nNam: What is the most fascinating aspect of this custom?\nMai: Anthropologists and participants are intrigued by hundred-meter wooden longhouses and enjoy gathering around the hearth.\nNam: How does it preserve cultural heritage or improve well-being?\nMai: It reinforces carved bird and lizard motifs and honors the spiritual value of Kpan seating bench.\nNam: Wonderful! That provides an insightful perspective on cultural diversity.",
      "clozeText": "Understanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Dak Lak plateau, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving hundred-meter wooden longhouses and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in gathering around the hearth, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating carved bird and lizard motifs helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing Kpan seating bench strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The Ede Matriarchal Heritage and Communal Longhouses exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Dak Lak plateau. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies hundred-meter wooden longhouses and reflects carved bird and lizard motifs, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in gathering around the hearth maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize Kpan seating bench as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nUnderstanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Dak Lak plateau, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving hundred-meter wooden longhouses and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in gathering around the hearth, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating carved bird and lizard motifs helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing Kpan seating bench strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Ede Matriarchal Heritage and Communal Longhouses exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Dak Lak plateau. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies hundred-meter wooden longhouses and reflects carved bird and lizard motifs, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in gathering around the hearth maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize Kpan seating bench as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Features of Dak Lak plateau; Key customs like hundred-meter wooden longhouses; Why Kpan seating bench is respected; Your reflection on preserving heritage.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, The Ede Matriarchal Heritage and Communal Longhouses is an extraordinary cultural treasure. Located in Dak Lak plateau, it embodies hundred-meter wooden longhouses and illustrates how communities harmoniously interact with their environment. Practicing gathering around the hearth instills profound moral values and preserves carved bird and lizard motifs. Moreover, honoring Kpan seating bench reinforces our ancestral roots. I believe youth should actively champion the preservation of this cherished heritage.",
