      "schoolName": "TRƯỜNG THCS ĐỒNG YÊN",
      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Phong: Hi Lan! What cultural tradition or lifestyle are you discussing in English class?\nLan: Hi Phong! I am presenting about Traditional Wedding Ceremonies in Southern Viet Nam at Mekong River delta.\nPhong: What is the most fascinating aspect of this custom?\nLan: Anthropologists and participants are intrigued by festive red betel areca trays and enjoy offering wedding gifts.\nPhong: How does it preserve cultural heritage or improve well-being?\nLan: It reinforces elaborate wedding processions and honors the spiritual value of traditional silk ao dai.\nPhong: Wonderful! That provides an insightful perspective on cultural diversity.",
      "clozeText": "Understanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Mekong River delta, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving festive red betel areca trays and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in offering wedding gifts, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating elaborate wedding processions helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing traditional silk ao dai strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Traditional Wedding Ceremonies in Southern Viet Nam exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Mekong River delta. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies festive red betel areca trays and reflects elaborate wedding processions, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in offering wedding gifts maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize traditional silk ao dai as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nUnderstanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Mekong River delta, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving festive red betel areca trays and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in offering wedding gifts, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating elaborate wedding processions helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing traditional silk ao dai strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTraditional Wedding Ceremonies in Southern Viet Nam exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Mekong River delta. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies festive red betel areca trays and reflects elaborate wedding processions, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in offering wedding gifts maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize traditional silk ao dai as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Features of Mekong River delta; Key customs like festive red betel areca trays; Why traditional silk ao dai is respected; Your reflection on preserving heritage.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Traditional Wedding Ceremonies in Southern Viet Nam is an extraordinary cultural treasure. Located in Mekong River delta, it embodies festive red betel areca trays and illustrates how communities harmoniously interact with their environment. Practicing offering wedding gifts instills profound moral values and preserves elaborate wedding processions. Moreover, honoring traditional silk ao dai reinforces our ancestral roots. I believe youth should actively champion the preservation of this cherished heritage.",
