      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Phong: Hi Lan! What historical milestone or wonder of Viet Nam are you presenting today?\nLan: Hi Phong! I am presenting about The Subterranean Splendor of Son Doong Cave at Phong Nha - Ke Bang national park.\nPhong: What is the most remarkable feature of this topic?\nLan: Historians and travelers are captivated by towering limestone dolines and intrigued by spelunking through colossal caverns.\nPhong: How does it illustrate Viet Nam's heritage or rapid modernization?\nLan: It highlights underground primordial rainforests and demonstrates the enduring value of subterranean river crossing.\nPhong: Outstanding! Your talk provides deep historical depth and national pride.",
      "clozeText": "Reflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Phong Nha - Ke Bang national park, historians and architects have meticulously studied towering limestone dolines to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in spelunking through colossal caverns, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving subterranean river crossing guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The Subterranean Splendor of Son Doong Cave serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Phong Nha - Ke Bang national park. Throughout decades of change, towering limestone dolines and underground primordial rainforests have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in spelunking through colossal caverns gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect subterranean river crossing to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nReflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Phong Nha - Ke Bang national park, historians and architects have meticulously studied towering limestone dolines to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in spelunking through colossal caverns, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving subterranean river crossing guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Subterranean Splendor of Son Doong Cave serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Phong Nha - Ke Bang national park. Throughout decades of change, towering limestone dolines and underground primordial rainforests have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in spelunking through colossal caverns gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect subterranean river crossing to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Historical context in Phong Nha - Ke Bang national park; Key features like towering limestone dolines; How spelunking through colossal caverns impacted society; Importance of subterranean river crossing.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, The Subterranean Splendor of Son Doong Cave offers a profound window into our nation's history. Located in Phong Nha - Ke Bang national park, it commemorates towering limestone dolines and reflects the incredible resilience of previous generations. Reflecting on spelunking through colossal caverns helps modern teenagers appreciate contemporary privileges while honoring underground primordial rainforests. Furthermore, safeguarding subterranean river crossing preserves our sacred national soul amidst rapid globalization. I am immensely proud of Viet Nam's historical legacy.",
