      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Phong: Hi Lan! What historical milestone or wonder of Viet Nam are you presenting today?\nLan: Hi Phong! I am presenting about Extended Three-Generation Families Living Together at traditional urban townhouse.\nPhong: What is the most remarkable feature of this topic?\nLan: Historians and travelers are captivated by sharing multigenerational stories and intrigued by eating dinner together.\nPhong: How does it illustrate Viet Nam's heritage or rapid modernization?\nLan: It highlights filial respect and family bonding and demonstrates the enduring value of ancestral wooden altar.\nPhong: Outstanding! Your talk provides deep historical depth and national pride.",
      "clozeText": "Reflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In traditional urban townhouse, historians and architects have meticulously studied sharing multigenerational stories to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in eating dinner together, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving ancestral wooden altar guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Extended Three-Generation Families Living Together serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with traditional urban townhouse. Throughout decades of change, sharing multigenerational stories and filial respect and family bonding have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in eating dinner together gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect ancestral wooden altar to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nReflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In traditional urban townhouse, historians and architects have meticulously studied sharing multigenerational stories to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in eating dinner together, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving ancestral wooden altar guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nExtended Three-Generation Families Living Together serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with traditional urban townhouse. Throughout decades of change, sharing multigenerational stories and filial respect and family bonding have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in eating dinner together gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect ancestral wooden altar to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Historical context in traditional urban townhouse; Key features like sharing multigenerational stories; How eating dinner together impacted society; Importance of ancestral wooden altar.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Extended Three-Generation Families Living Together offers a profound window into our nation's history. Located in traditional urban townhouse, it commemorates sharing multigenerational stories and reflects the incredible resilience of previous generations. Reflecting on eating dinner together helps modern teenagers appreciate contemporary privileges while honoring filial respect and family bonding. Furthermore, safeguarding ancestral wooden altar preserves our sacred national soul amidst rapid globalization. I am immensely proud of Viet Nam's historical legacy.",
