      "schoolName": "TRƯỜNG THCS ĐỒNG YÊN",
      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_ck1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Phong: Hi Lan! What historical milestone or wonder of Viet Nam are you presenting today?\nLan: Hi Phong! I am presenting about The Historic Long Bien Bridge Over the Red River at Red River crossing.\nPhong: What is the most remarkable feature of this topic?\nLan: Historians and travelers are captivated by riveted steel cantilever spans and intrigued by watching river barges pass.\nPhong: How does it illustrate Viet Nam's heritage or rapid modernization?\nLan: It highlights peaceful pedestrian walkways and demonstrates the enduring value of century-old railway track.\nPhong: Outstanding! Your talk provides deep historical depth and national pride.",
      "clozeText": "Reflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Red River crossing, historians and architects have meticulously studied riveted steel cantilever spans to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in watching river barges pass, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving century-old railway track guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The Historic Long Bien Bridge Over the Red River serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Red River crossing. Throughout decades of change, riveted steel cantilever spans and peaceful pedestrian walkways have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in watching river barges pass gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect century-old railway track to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nReflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Red River crossing, historians and architects have meticulously studied riveted steel cantilever spans to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in watching river barges pass, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving century-old railway track guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Historic Long Bien Bridge Over the Red River serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Red River crossing. Throughout decades of change, riveted steel cantilever spans and peaceful pedestrian walkways have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in watching river barges pass gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect century-old railway track to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Historical context in Red River crossing; Key features like riveted steel cantilever spans; How watching river barges pass impacted society; Importance of century-old railway track.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, The Historic Long Bien Bridge Over the Red River offers a profound window into our nation's history. Located in Red River crossing, it commemorates riveted steel cantilever spans and reflects the incredible resilience of previous generations. Reflecting on watching river barges pass helps modern teenagers appreciate contemporary privileges while honoring peaceful pedestrian walkways. Furthermore, safeguarding century-old railway track preserves our sacred national soul amidst rapid globalization. I am immensely proud of Viet Nam's historical legacy.",
